  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The State of Mississippi has received $57.8M in federal contract obligations so far in FY2027. The award count stands at 1,427 and the average award size is $40.5K. Obligations fell 99.1% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show prior peaks well above the current year: FY22 recorded $5B, FY23 recorded $8.7B, FY24 recorded $6.3B, FY25 recorded $8B, and FY26 recorded $6.3B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in FY2027 to date, obligating $44.7M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $6.5M and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $2.9M. Cut Stone and Stone Product Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $10.3M, and Computer Systems Design Services follows at $6.7M. Top vendors include COLUMBUS MARBLE WORKS, INC. at $6.8M, SPATIAL FRONT INC at $6.5M, and PARAMOUNT CONSTRUCTION GROUP, LLC at $4.9M. These figures reflect fiscal-year-to-date totals and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are buying in Mississippi?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $44.7M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $6.5M and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $2.9M. The Department of Justice obligated $1.9M and the Department of Labor obligated $998K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest vendors and which industries lead?",
        "body": "COLUMBUS MARBLE WORKS, INC. received $6.8M and SPATIAL FRONT INC received $6.5M in FY2027 to date. Cut Stone and Stone Product Manufacturing leads industries with $10.3M and Computer Systems Design Services follows with $6.7M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction received $4.9M and Security Guards and Patrol Services received $3.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
